Example.Input:
Java (OOP, strongly typed):
```java
{{
public class Counter {
    private int count = 0;
    public void increment() { count++; }
    public int getCount() { return count; }
}
}}
```

C++ (procedural, index-based iteration):
```cpp
{{
for (int i = 0; i < arr.size(); i++) {
    printf("Index %d: %d\n", i, arr[i]);
}
}}
```

ConditionalLogic.Condition:
IF source is Java or C# THEN map getter/setter pairs to
        @property; checked exceptions to try/except; generics to type hints;
        interface to Protocol; abstract class to ABC; builder pattern to
        dataclass with defaults; verbose null checks to truthiness or
        "x or default".
